<title>YUGOSLAVIA: SOCCER-YUGOSLAVIA BEAT CZECH REPUBLIC 3-0 IN EURO UNDER-21.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-YUGOSLAVIA BEAT CZECH REPUBLIC 3-0 IN EURO UNDER-21.</headline>
<dateline>NOVI SAD, Yugoslavia 1996-11-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia beat the</p>
<p>Czech Republic 3-0 (halftime 2-0) in a European under-21 soccer</p>
<p>championship group six qualifier on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Ivan Tomic 25, Dragan Isailovic 34, Damir Stojak</p>
<p>90.</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,500</p>
<p>Standings (tabulated - played, won, drawn, lost, goals for,</p>
<p>goals against, points):</p>
<p> Yugoslavia	     2   2   0   0   4   0   6</p>
<p> Slovakia		 1   1   0   0   3   0   3</p>
<p> Spain		    1   1   0   0   2   1   3</p>
<p> Czech Rebublic	 3   1   0   2   5   5   3</p>
<p> Malta		    3   0   0   3   0   8   0</p>
<p>Next match: November 12, Spain v Slovakia.</p>
</text>
